To compute the factorial of a number iteratively in Java, we can initialize a variable `result` to 1 and then multiply it by each integer from 2 to the given number (n). Here is an example code snippet:
```
public static long factorialIterative(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) return 1;
    long result = 1;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        result *= i;
    }
    return result;
}
```
